---
// One-off system diagram for the telecom-event-platform case study. Theme-aware
// via CSS custom properties (inherits the page's light/dark tokens, no JS).
---

<figure class="arch">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 880 300"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="arch-title arch-desc"
    class="arch__svg"
  >
    <title id="arch-title">Telecom Event Management Platform — system architecture</title>
    <desc id="arch-desc">
      The Flutter field app and the Next.js admin console both call Nginx over HTTPS.
      Nginx routes to the Go REST API, which is guarded by JWT and RBAC middleware.
      The API reads and writes PostgreSQL and uploads files to AWS S3. Nginx, the API,
      and PostgreSQL run together in one Docker Compose stack on a single EC2 host.
    </desc>

    <defs>
      <marker id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="arch__arrowhead" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <!-- Docker Compose / EC2 boundary -->
    <rect x="270" y="20" width="420" height="220" rx="10" class="arch__boundary" />
    <text x="286" y="42" class="arch__boundary-label">Docker Compose · EC2 (ap-southeast-1)</text>

    <!-- Clients -->
    <g class="arch__node">
      <rect x="16" y="40" width="170" height="58" rx="8" />
      <text x="101" y="64" class="arch__label">Flutter</text>
      <text x="101" y="82" class="arch__sublabel">Field app · BLoC</text>
    </g>

    <g class="arch__node">
      <rect x="16" y="196" width="170" height="58" rx="8" />
      <text x="101" y="220" class="arch__label">Next.js Admin</text>
      <text x="101" y="238" class="arch__sublabel">React 19 · MUI</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Nginx -->
    <g class="arch__node arch__node--infra">
      <rect x="300" y="88" width="110" height="86" rx="8" />
      <text x="355" y="126" class="arch__label">Nginx</text>
      <text x="355" y="144" class="arch__sublabel">TLS · routing</text>
    </g>

    <!-- API -->
    <g class="arch__node arch__node--infra">
      <rect x="460" y="70" width="190" height="120" rx="8" />
      <text x="555" y="106" class="arch__label">Go REST API</text>
      <text x="555" y="126" class="arch__sublabel">REST → Service → Repo</text>
      <text x="555" y="144" class="arch__sublabel">sqlx · golang-migrate</text>
      <text x="555" y="162" class="arch__sublabel">JWT (HS256) · RBAC</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Data stores -->
    <g class="arch__node arch__node--infra">
      <rect x="700" y="30" width="150" height="56" rx="8" />
      <text x="775" y="54" class="arch__label">PostgreSQL</text>
      <text x="775" y="72" class="arch__sublabel">events, staff, kit</text>
    </g>

    <g class="arch__node">
      <rect x="700" y="176" width="150" height="56" rx="8" />
      <text x="775" y="200" class="arch__label">AWS S3</text>
      <text x="775" y="218" class="arch__sublabel">uploads, exports</text>
    </g>

    <!-- Edges -->
    <path d="M186,69 L300,110" class="arch__edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
    <path d="M186,225 L300,152" class="arch__edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
    <text x="225" y="90" class="arch__edge-label">HTTPS</text>
    <text x="225" y="215" class="arch__edge-label">HTTPS</text>

    <path d="M410,130 L460,130" class="arch__edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />

    <path d="M650,110 L700,66" class="arch__edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
    <path d="M650,150 L700,196" class="arch__edge" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="arch__caption">
    Both clients reach the API only through Nginx; JWT + RBAC middleware gates every
    write. Nginx, the API, and Postgres run as one Docker Compose stack on a single
    EC2 host — S3 is the one external AWS service.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .arch {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
  }
  .arch__svg {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }
  .arch__boundary {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
  }
  .arch__boundary-label {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .arch__node rect {
    fill: var(--bg-raised);
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .arch__node--infra rect {
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }
  .arch__label {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .arch__sublabel {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .arch__edge {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--text-muted);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  .arch__edge-label {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 10px;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .arch__arrowhead {
    fill: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .arch__caption {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
